  "title": "Training Time Comparison",
  "caption": "Mean seconds to fit one fold, per model and per run, on a log scale. Whiskers span the observed minimum and maximum across that run's folds rather than a standard deviation, because the quantity is not symmetric: an ensemble fold whose member search picked a large gradient-boosting configuration costs an order of magnitude more than one that picked a small one. These are the times the project's own runs recorded on a machine that was sometimes running other jobs; T26's controlled bench is the like-for-like comparison. The colourblind-safe palette holds eight colours and there are ten runs, so the last two are hatched rather than given a ninth colour.",
